# Feast Feature Store - xFusionCorp Industries Fraud Detection

This repository contains the scaffolded Feast feature store repository and training pipelines for the xFusionCorp Industries fraud-detection workflow.

## Project Structure

```text
/root/code/
├── build_training_set.py             # Script to generate point-in-time training sets
├── training_set.parquet              # Output training dataset
└── feature_repo/
    └── feature_repo/
        ├── feature_store.yaml        # Feast project configuration (provider, registry, offline store)
        ├── feature_definitions.py    # Starter feature definitions & views
        ├── data/
        │   ├── registry.db           # SQLite local registry generated via `feast apply`
        │   └── driver_stats.parquet  # Parquet source data for driver statistics
        └── __init__.py
Quick Start Guide
1. Initialize the Feature Repository
If initializing from scratch:

Bash
cd /root/code/
feast init feature_repo
2. Apply Feature Definitions
Apply the local feature definitions to populate the SQLite registry:

Bash
cd /root/code/feature_repo/feature_repo
feast apply
3. Build the Point-in-Time Training Set
Run the pre-staged python script to retrieve historical features using a point-in-time join and save the output dataset:

Bash
python /root/code/build_training_set.py
4. Run the Feast UI
Start the web dashboard to inspect entities, feature views, and data sources:

Bash
cd /root/code/feature_repo/feature_repo
feast ui &
Access the dashboard locally at http://localhost:8888.


